This licence applies to every file in the ee/ directory of the HexProcure
repository and to nothing else. All files outside ee/ are licensed under the
MIT licence in the root LICENSE file.

1. Definitions

"Software" means the files in the ee/ directory and any copy or modification
of them. "Licence Key" means a signed token issued by HexProcure and verified
by the check in src/lib/license.ts. "Licensor" means HexProcure.

2. Grant to view, modify and contribute

You may view, copy and modify the Software, and you may send contributions to
the Licensor, for the purposes of evaluation, development, testing and
contribution. This grant needs no Licence Key.

3. Production use needs a licence key

You may use the Software in production only while you hold a valid Licence Key
for the tier that covers the feature you use. "Production" means any use that
is not evaluation, development or testing, including use for your own business
or for your customers. A Licence Key is personal to its licensee and may not be
shared or resold.

4. No circumvention

You may not remove, disable, weaken or work around the licence check, the
feature tier map, or any notice that identifies the Software as licensed. You
may not generate, forge or modify a Licence Key.

5. No redistribution as a standalone product

You may not sell, sublicense or distribute the Software, or a product that
substantially consists of it, as a standalone offering or as part of a
competing hosted service. You may distribute copies that keep this licence and
all notices intact, such as a fork made for contribution.

6. Contributions

Contributions to ee/ are accepted under this licence. By sending a
contribution you confirm the Developer Certificate of Origin (see
CONTRIBUTING.md) and grant the Licensor the right to use, relicense and
distribute it as part of the Software.

7. Termination

This licence ends automatically if you breach it. On termination you must stop
production use of the Software and delete your copies used in production. The
Licensor may revoke a Licence Key for non-payment or breach. Sections 4, 5, 8
and 9 survive termination.

8. No warranty

The Software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or
implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose and
non-infringement.

9. Limitation of liability

To the extent the law allows, the Licensor is not liable for any indirect or
consequential loss, or for any claim in excess of the fees you paid in the
twelve months before the claim arose.

10. General

This licence is the whole agreement about the Software. If a part is
unenforceable, the rest stays in force. Questions and licence keys:
licensing@hexprocure.dev (placeholder, founder confirms).
